PR explicitly replaces that guarantee (\"this replaces the previous guarantee that a better-matching menu entry beats a weaker app match\"). Under the PR, the reporter's requested order is the specified one. The rewrite is our proof work (eec40e87), not upstream's. I re-ran it at a058df8b and it passes. Auditor notes rdec-ff7b8275/-390ed256 are not approvals.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":68},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Compat cf-84c887f1e7521d90: #10340 report test rewritten to reporter-expectation mode (unapproved)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"/^ok: 'Chrome' .../m is replaced by /^MET: the installed app ranks first/m. The m-flag anchor semantics are unchanged; only the expected verdict text changes, following SJ7P. The inventory classifies it intended_change (SJ7P). It still awaits a human approval; auditor notes rdec-3ef3d7a0/-8b63c087 are notes.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":69},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Compat cf-8e9a9ac64c8e7fac: removed /^...$/m expected-line regex in the #10340 test (unapproved)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"The base call inherited process.env implicitly. The head passes { ...process.env, ...env }, which is still the full environment plus REPORT_ASSERT for #10340. cwd, shell and buffering are unchanged. It is test-helper code, not product code. The inventory classifies it intended_change (SJ7P). It awaits human approval; auditor notes rdec-e3eb6e64/-e50f28b5 are notes.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":22},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Compat cf-e51dfadbcda62f32: runReport now passes an env overlay to spawnSync (unapproved)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Upstream (1bb6c3c9) changed menu-test.sh:473. The old assertion was `rankScore('style.font','font') < rankScore('apps.fontforge','font')` ('menu keeps a better-matching menu entry above a weaker app match'). It now asserts the reverse. The proof-side copy at menumodel-replay.test.mjs:413 is inverted the same way, outside any test() block. review.compat test_diff reports '2 existing test file(s) changed' and flags neither inversion, so no compat approval gate covers this retired guarantee. The PR states the inversion verbatim (\"replaces the previous guarantee ... (`style.font` vs `apps.fontforge` for `font`)\"). It is intended, but a human reviewer should approve it explicitly, the same way as cf-6ea9f79aa0b1c1de. This is my reading of the diff; the engine has no record for it.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":473},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":413},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Upstream inverted an existing assertion in test/shell.d/menu-test.sh; no compat finding records it","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.behaviorDiff ran 213 inputs over 5 partitions (corpus 17, data 176, lifecycle 14, scale 3, timing 3) with 0 differences. test/bdiff/harness.mjs drives JSONC parsing and the menu request lifecycle. Neither path calls searchScore or rebuildDisplay with a query, so the result says nothing about whether ranking is unchanged. I ran base 8418e7c8 vs head a058df8b rebuildDisplay myself under node vm with the shipped menu (scratch only). vsc: base `setup.default.editor.vscode, install.editor.vscode, apps.code`, head `apps.code | ...`. system: `system | apps.btop` becomes `apps.btop | system`. Root tu without apps is identical. The earlier manual differential (bdiff/12223.md) found 4 intended buckets and 1 unclassified (the divider). Those results are outside the package, so no behavior_changed claim can be typed.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"severity":"medium","title":"The differential found no difference, but its harness does not exercise search ranking","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay","shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"root search for 'system' with btop installed (GenericName System Monitor, Keywords system): Enter runs apps.btop instead of the exact-label System menu"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"At a058df8b with the shipped default menu, a root search for `system` puts apps.btop (aliases system/process/task) above the menu entry labelled exactly System, so Enter opens btop. The bias decides this and the pinning in rebuildDisplay reinforces it. The PR discloses the general tradeoff but not the exact-label case. The mirror's witness pins only the description-only form ('update', menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1418). A maintainer decision is needed.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: should a keyword-only app match beat an exact-label menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'tu' with one installed app matching: the divider between direct children (setup) and deeper entries (install.tui) is no longer drawn"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Base, root `tu`: `setup | install.tui ... apps.code ...`. Head: `apps.code | setup install.tui ...`. The current-menu rows and the deeper rows now share one section. The PR says only \"with the divider following them\". Our TKDP rewrite (\"one divider separates the apps from all menu entries\") and the witness at menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1406 codify the new form. That is our reading, not the author's statement.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":709},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is dropping the direct/deeper divider whenever an app matches intended?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'e' with 200 installed apps: index of the first menu row in the result list"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Every matching app now precedes every menu row. The earlier manual differential measured the first menu row for a one-letter query at index 20 with 20 apps, 56 with 63 and 179 with 200 (base: index 0). The PR screenshots show one-app cases only.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: with many installed apps, do short queries bury every menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Burial at scale\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"property: for every tier value and kind, max app score*1000+depth*25+order < min menu/link score*1000"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The invariant \"exceeds every match tier\" exists only in a comment. A future tier at 98 or above would silently let a menu row outrank an app. The MC/DC replay pins today's values, not the invariant.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does the -100 bias stay above every tier if a tier >= 98 is added? (opinion: name the constant)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Tier-gap invariant property test\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"The disclosure's only source record is test:shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:233:item. That is the product accessor `function item(id)` under `// Implements: SW-REQ-260929-B8N9`, not a test. In engine build 650534c2, pkg/mcdc/show.go annotationScanTestLikeName treats any declaration whose name starts with \"it\" as test-like. So item() becomes a zero-scenario witness that can never get a JUnit outcome. item() is outside this PR's hunks (Menu.qml:695-713), and B8N9 reaches the change only through the file-level Menu.qml trace. Its real witness, test/shell.d/menu-pointer-lifecycle-test.sh, passed. B8N9 shows 2 passed and 1 unknown, with all 3 obligation cells observed_pass. The disclosure still prevents readiness until the engine heuristic is fixed upstream (reqforge) or the record is otherwise resolved. A review cannot clear it.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":233},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-pointer-lifecycle-test.sh","kind":"file","line":7},{"id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"test_outcome_unobserved:SW-REQ-260929-B8N9 comes from a non-test that the scanner treats as a test (pre-existing, not this PR)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Since the previous review, the baseline runs test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh and menu-acceptance-test.sh in a headless sway. Both appear in review.tests with outcome passed, so the old 10 test_outcome_unobserved disclosures are gone. testResults: ingested, current, 56 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped. Of the 73 obligation cells in claimEvidence, 39 are observed_pass and 34 are not_linked (no test tagged with that class). The not_linked cells are not tested evidence.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-acceptance-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Live-session menu tests now have observed outcomes (menu-live suite)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this JS/QML change. The empty spec-gap list therefore proves nothing about uncodified connections (review.scope approximations). From reading the code: searchScore's only callers are the Menu.qml searchScore() wrapper, which feeds rebuildDisplay, plus test assertions; resolveRoute does not use it. These are reading facts, not engine-verified facts.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable); uncodified connections cannot be detected","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:c5ab789e1642d18fb4de0f1755946578d26787d8e51e3eaa2b74ead7eb10110b","packageIdentity":"epkg-1455189af54c0cc41cf665e959447312840255a84e8c9f6350a668d51312cce7","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"The change deliberately reorders every menu search, and Enter's target changes for many queries, including exact-label menu entries. It carries 4 unapproved compatibility changes plus an inverted upstream assertion that no compat finding records. The configured differential does not exercise ranking. The engine's risk is low on gates and coverage. This assessment is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":9,"rationale":"Pins the maintainer's decision either way. Root 'system' with btop installed, and 'terminal' with Alacritty: assert which row is first.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1418}],"title":"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app"},{"forClaim":10,"rationale":"For root 'tu' with one matching app, assert the boundary count and position. This turns the divider change into a decided, pinned behaviour.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406}],"title":"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present"},{"forClaim":11,"rationale":"With 200 synthetic app rows, record the index of the first menu row for one-letter queries and assert a bound the maintainer accepts.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"title":"Burial at scale"},{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"Enumerate tiers x kinds x realistic depth/order and assert app max < menu min. It fails loudly if a tier >= 98 is added.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377}],"title":"Tier-gap invariant property test"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #12223 (ax1g) makes installed apps rank above menu entries in menu search (upstream commit 1bb6c3c9 on the mirror). It changes two things. First, the `searchScore` app bias goes from -5 to -100 (MenuModel.js:377). That exceeds the whole tier range, so any matching app outranks any matching menu entry. Second, `rebuildDisplay` pins matching app rows above the current menu's rows and recomputes the divider (Menu.qml:695-713). The PR also edits test/shell.d/menu-test.sh: a new `vsc` test and an inverted cross-tier assertion. Later mirror commits are our proof work, not upstream: SJ7P/TKDP rewritten to the PR's intent, rebuildDisplay witnesses, the #10340 test in reporter-expectation mode, citation re-points, REVIEW-261001-EAD8/-ER1B, a KI note, a trace re-review.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Changed decisions are measured: 2/2 covered, 0 uncovered lines or outcomes. 56 ingested test results: 56 passed, 0 failed. I re-ran both node suites at a058df8b: 30 passed, 1 unrelated skip (#10601 needs Qt). I also ran base vs head `rebuildDisplay`: for `vsc` VS Code comes first, for `system` btop sits above the exact-label System menu, and at root `tu` the direct/deeper divider moves below the app.\n\n**Compatibility.** There are 4 unapproved compat changes (compat_change_unapproved, prevents ready). Two are test_diff changes: the replay MC/DC values and the #10340 rewrite. Two are removed-behaviour items in that test's helper. All four follow the PR's stated intent. The auditor's \"accept\" notes are notes, not approvals; only a human reviewer approves. The differential ran 213 inputs with no difference, but its harness does not exercise search ranking.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Should a keyword-only app beat an exact-label menu entry? (2) Is dropping the direct/deeper divider when an app matches intended? (3) Can many apps bury menu entries?\n\n**Traceability.** SJ7P and TKDP were modified; 39 more are code_changed through file-level traces. No spec-gap candidates, but effects were not analyzed, so uncodified connections could not be detected.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** test_outcome_unobserved:SW-REQ-260929-B8N9 still prevents readiness. Its source is the unchanged product function `item()` (Menu.qml:233), which the engine's scanner takes for a test because its name starts with \"it\". Readiness is not_assessed; next decision is human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved)."}
